<task id="AIR2-072" project="spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Cross-satellite seam-fork verification — core is the only modifier of Services/Ai/ internals</title>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <phase>H — G-R2-D Hardening</phase>
    <gate>G-R2-D (hardening)</gate>
    <estimated-effort>0.5 day</estimated-effort>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Verification-only sweep (grep + NetArchTest) with a clear pass/fail rule; but effort=high because a real fork is a cross-project architectural violation whose detection needs careful, low-false-positive analysis.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <goal-eligible>true</goal-eligible>
    <tags>bff-api, hardening, seam-boundary, cross-project, adr-013, adr-039</tags>
    <dependencies>none (Wave H; reads satellite state at gate time)</dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Verify that no satellite project (Compose r2, Insights Engine refurbish) forked an AI-internal seam — the core is the ONLY project that modifies `Services/Ai/` internals; satellites consume only through `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` (spec FR-D-03, ADR-013). Enforce with a grep + NetArchTest check and cross-check the hot-path registry / `/conflict-check`. This is a verification-and-enforcement task, not a refactor.
  </prompt>

  <role>Architecture-conformance engineer fluent in the Spaarke AI seam boundary (ADR-013 PublicContracts facade), NetArchTest, and the cross-project hot-path registry.</role>

  <goal>
    A grep/NetArchTest check confirms (a) satellites reference AI capability only via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`, never AI-internal types, and (b) no satellite worktree contains a divergent copy of a core seam. The check is codified (a NetArchTest rule and/or a documented grep recipe) so it re-runs at future gates. The hot-path registry + `/conflict-check` are reconciled: the core is recorded as the sole `Services/Ai/` internal modifier.
  </goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="spec">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/spec.md</file>
    <file purpose="plan">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/plan.md</file>
    <file purpose="hot-path-registry">projects/INDEX.md</file>
    <file purpose="bff-governance">.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    <file purpose="satellite-design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/design.md</file>
  </inputs>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">CRUD/satellite consumers reach AI only via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; no injecting `IOpenAiClient`/`IPlaybookService` or other AI-internal types.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">No second dispatch protocol / forked seam; the one grounded-execution surface is core-owned.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Core is the SOLE modifier of `Services/Ai/` internals; satellites consume, never fork (design §0.3 C-3).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Any codified check is a KEEP-path arch test; no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>architecture/seam-boundary, publiccontracts, netarchtest, hot-path-registry</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Seam facade" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/">The only sanctioned satellite consumption surface; the check asserts satellites touch nothing under `Services/Ai/` outside this folder.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Hot-path registry" location="projects/INDEX.md">Records which worktrees touch BFF / SpaarkeAi; reconcile that only core is marked as an AI-internal modifier.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Conflict-check" location=".claude/skills/conflict-check/">Auto-invoked before BFF PRs; this task confirms it flags any satellite seam-fork.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <context>
    <background>R2 core publishes seams (Phase A0) that Compose r2 and the future Insights refurbish consume. The risk is a satellite copying/forking a seam locally instead of consuming the PublicContracts facade, which would silently diverge. This task makes that structurally detectable.</background>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="n/a">Runs at gate time against whatever satellite state exists; no code prerequisite.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
    <related-work>
      <item>Compose r2 already re-based onto core seams (2026-07-08); this verifies it stayed re-based.</item>
      <item>Task 079 (G-R2-D verification) cites the seam-fork check result.</item>
    </related-work>
  </context>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Enumerate seams">List the R2-published seam types under `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` + the AI-internal namespaces that MUST NOT be referenced externally.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Grep sweep">Grep the satellite worktrees for references to AI-internal types + for divergent copies of seam DTOs.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Codify">Add a NetArchTest rule (or documented grep recipe) asserting satellites depend only on PublicContracts; place it in the KEEP-path arch tests.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Registry reconcile">Confirm projects/INDEX.md marks core as the sole `Services/Ai/` internal modifier; confirm `/conflict-check` would flag a fork.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Report">Record findings (zero forks expected) in the project notes as gate evidence.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="rg">Grep the satellite worktrees for AI-internal references</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Run the NetArchTest arch test</tool>
    <tool name="git">Commit the codified check on the project branch</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/ (NetArchTest seam-boundary rule) or a documented grep recipe under project notes</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/notes/ (seam-fork verification report)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A grep/NetArchTest check confirms satellites reference AI capability only via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`, never AI-internal types.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No satellite worktree contains a divergent copy of a core seam DTO (sweep evidence recorded).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The check is codified so it re-runs at future gates (NetArchTest rule or documented recipe committed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">projects/INDEX.md records the core as the sole `Services/Ai/` internal modifier; `/conflict-check` would flag a fork.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a deliberately-seeded satellite reference to an AI-internal type is caught by the check (fails as designed).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a real seam-fork is found in a satellite worktree, STOP — this is a cross-project architectural violation (ADR-013/ADR-039). Surface it to the operator with the offending file:line rather than silently patching the satellite (satellite fixes are out of core scope).</trigger>
  </escalation>
</task>
